    "title": "Women's March Madness full schedule: NCAA Tournament dates, times, TV info",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 11:30 p.m. ETThis story has been updated with new information.The women’s NCAA basketball tournament will get underway soon, with 68 teams competing for a chance to call themselves the national champions.Azzi Fudd and the UConn Huskies were announced as the No. 1 overall seed in the tournament. Lauren Betts and UCLA will serve as the No. 2 overall seed in the tournament. The Bruins will take on Cal Baptist from Riverside, California in the first round.The last four teams seeded among the 68 will compete in the “First Four” play-in round. The winner of those games will join the rest of the field in first-round action.The top 16 seeds will host the first weekend of games that will make up the first and second rounds.Teams competing in the Sweet 16 and the Elite Eight will play in either Fort Worth, Texas, or Sacramento, California.The Final Four teams will gather at the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix to determine the champion.2026 Women's March Madness schedule: Times, Dates, TV channel for NCAA TournamentAll times are EasternWednesday, March 18First Four GamesREGIONAL 2: No. 11 Nebraska vs. No. 11 Richmond | 7 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 3: No. 16 Stephen F. Austin vs. No. 16 Missouri State | 9 p.m. | ESPN2Thursday, March 19First Four GamesREGIONAL 4: No. 16 Southern vs. No. 16 Samford | 7 p.m. | ESPN2 REGIONAL 4: No. 10 Arizona State vs. No. 10 Virginia | 9 p.m. | ESPN2Friday, March 20Round of 64REGIONAL 2: No. 14 Charleston vs. No. 3 Duke | 11:30 a.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 4: No. 14 UC San Diego vs. No. 3 TCU | Noon | ESPNREGIONAL 3: No. 9 Virginia Tech vs. No. 8 Oregon | 1:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 2: No. 11 Nebraska/Richmond vs. No. 6 Baylor | 2 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 4: No. 11 South Dakota St. vs. No. 6 Washington | 2:30 p.m. | ESPNEWSREGIONAL 1: No. 12 Murray State vs. No. 5 Maryland | 3 p.m. | ESPNUREGIONAL 2: No. 12 Gonzaga vs. No. 5 Ole Miss | 3:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 3: No. 16 Missouri State/SFA vs. No. 1 Texas | 4 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 3: No. 15 Holy Cross vs. No. 2 Michigan | 5:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 1: No. 13 Western Illinois vs. No. 4 North Carolina | 5:30 p.m. | ESPNEWSREGIONAL 2: No. 15 Jacksonville vs. No. 2 LSU | 6 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 2: No. 13 Green Bay vs. No. 4 Minnesota | 6 p.m. | ESPNUREGIONAL 4: No. 12 Colorado State vs. No. 5 Michigan State | 7:30 p.m. | ESPNEWSREGIONAL 3: No. 10 Tennessee vs. No. 7 NC State | 8 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 2: No. 10 Villanova vs. No. 7 Texas Tech | 8:30 p.m. | ESPNUREGIONAL 4: No. 13 Idaho vs. No. 4 Oklahoma | 10 p.m. | ESPNSaturday, March 21Round of 64REGIONAL 1: No. 14 Howard vs. No. 3 Ohio State | 11:30 a.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 3: No. 14 Vermont vs. No. 3 Louisville | Noon | ESPNREGIONAL 4: No. 16 Southern U./Samford vs. No. 1 South Carolina | 1 p.m. | ABCREGIONAL 4: No. 10 Virginia/Arizona State vs. No. 7 Georgia | 1:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 1: No. 11 Fairfield vs. No. 6 Notre Dame | 2 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 3: No. 12 James Madison vs. No. 5 Kentucky | 2:30 p.m. | ESPNUREGIONAL 3: No. 11 Rhode Island vs. No. 6 Alabama | 2:30 p.m. | ESPNEWSREGIONAL 1: No. 16 UTSA vs. No. 1 UConn | 3 p.m. | ABCREGIONAL 4: No. 9 USC vs. No. 8 Clemson | 3:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 4: No. 15 Fairleigh Dickinson vs. No. 2 Iowa | 4 p.m. | ESPNREGIONAL 3: No. 13 Miami (OH) vs. No. 4 West Virginia | 5 p.m. | ESPNUREGIONAL 1: No. 9 Syracuse vs. No. 8 Iowa State | 5:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 1: No. 15 High Point vs. No. 2 Vanderbilt | 7 p.m. | ESPNEWSREGIONAL 2: No. 9 Princeton vs. No. 8 Oklahoma State | 7:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 1: No. 10 Colorado vs. No. 7 Illinois | 9:30 p.m. | ESPN2REGIONAL 2: No. 16 Cal Baptist vs. No. 1 UCLA | 10 p.m. | ESPNSunday, March 22Round of 32 Games: Times and TV channels TBDMonday, March 23Round of 32 Games: Times and TV channels TBDFriday, March 27Sweet 16 Games (Fort Worth, Texas and Sacramento): Times and TV channels TBDSaturday, March 28Sweet 16 Games (Fort Worth, Texas and Sacramento): Times and TV channels TBDSunday, March 29Elite Eight/Regional Final Games (Fort Worth, Texas and Sacramento): Times and TV channels TBDMonday, March 30Elite Eight/Regional Final Games (Fort Worth, Texas and Sacramento): Times and TV channels TBDFriday, April 3Final Four: 7 p.m. with the second semifinal starting 30 minutes after the first game ends. Both will be at Mortgage Matchup Center in PhoenixSunday, April 5NCAA championship game: 3:30 p.m. ET on ABC, hosted at Mortgage Matchup Center in PhoenixWomen's March Madness favorites by oddsOdds via BetMGM (as of Sunday morning)Connecticut: -275UCLA: +600Texas: +650South Carolina: +900LSU: +1700Vanderbilt: +5000Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
